From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] libwifi: 937 - enumerate MLD stations via hostapd unconditionally

iface_get_sta_info_band() only consulted hostapd when the nl80211 GET_STATION
read succeeded. On open mt76 an MLO fronthaul client is attributed to the
affiliated-link netdev, so a dump on the MLD netdev returns nothing and the
nl80211 read fails -- which then skipped the (working) hostapd ctrl query.
Result: wifi.apmld.<mld> stations returned empty even though the clients were
associated (assoclist, built from the hostapd cache, saw them fine).

Consult hostapd unconditionally (nl80211 best-effort, hostapd authoritative)
and treat the station as found if either source yields it. This lets
iface_get_mlsta_4addr_info populate every link so the apmld stations reply
carries per-link data, which map-agent (patch 986) then enumerates.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
+++ b/libwifi/modules/default/wifi.c
@@ -1464,12 +1464,25 @@
 	info->band = band;
 
 	ret = nlwifi_get_sta_info_band(iface, band, addr, info);
+	{
+		int hret;
+
+		/* nl80211 GET_STATION is best-effort here: on mt76 a dump on the
+		 * MLD netdev returns nothing for an MLO client (it is attributed
+		 * to the affiliated-link netdev), so gating hostapd on nl80211
+		 * success discarded the good data and MLD clients never enumerated.
+		 * hostapd ctrl is authoritative -- consult it unconditionally and
+		 * treat the station as found if either source yields it. */
+		hret = hostapd_cli_iface_get_sta_info(ctrl_iface, addr, info);
+		if (ret && !hret)
+			ret = 0;
+	}
+
 	if (!ret) {
 		uint16_t ap_width, sta_width;
 		enum wifi_bw ap_bw;
 
-		ret = hostapd_cli_iface_get_sta_info(ctrl_iface, addr, info);
-		if (!ret && info->rate.m.bw == 0) {
+		if (info->rate.m.bw == 0) {
 			WARN_ON(nlwifi_get_band_channel(iface, band, &ch, &ap_bw));
 
 			ap_width = wifi_bw_enum2MHz(ap_bw);
@@ -1481,9 +1494,7 @@
 		}
 
 		info->oper_std = wifi_standard_from_caps(ifname, band, &info->caps);
-	}
 
-	if (!ret) {
 		bw = wifi_bw_to_enum_bw(info->rate.m.bw);
 		info->maxrate = wifi_get_estimated_throughput(80, bw, &info->caps, info->rate.m.nss, 0);
 	}
